    The compiled checker shares context-free subtype and exclusion answers per trait table, so a bound list naming Number's closed family is checked in minutes, not past the count stage's limit (row 688)

    TypeAnalyzer's memos key each question by the whole cycle history and live on one analyzer, and the checker builds a fresh analyzer for every generic declaration, overload comparison and schema operation, so a question that names no type variable was computed again at every depth and in every analyzer: under the array family's two-trait bound the count stage's checker spent about 17 minutes in checkApi FortressLibrary, past its 900 s limit (row 688; explorations/compile-ladder/rung-array-bound/REPORT.md section 7). A memo on TraitTable now holds every True or False answer whose computation read neither the kind environment nor the cycle history (history lookups, staticParam, withClauseParams' scope test, an analyzer memo hit and a normalize-memo entry computed with such reads count as context reads), behind the switch fortress.analyzer.ground.cache, default on, beside fortress.analyzer.clauses.cache; every answer is the one the analyzer computes.

    Evidence: explorations/perf-probes/checker-speed/REPORT.md sections 2, 3, 6 and 7 (count stage 1,432 s to 371 s and distance stage 4,551 s to 1,885 s on a shadow with the library half on, answers identical site by site, 22.3M memo hits audited without a mismatch) and section 8 (the two tests); its skeptic's read, explorations/perf-probes/checker-speed/SKEPTIC.md, approved with fixes of style and test coverage, none changing an answer, none applied here. Tests: XXXBoundCheckSameNameTwoScopes (a context-dependent answer is not shared; red on a variant sharing every answer) and OverloadTwoBoundsClosedFamily. Landed from explorations/perf-probes/checker-speed/fix.patch (c5098915c) outside a batch, at the curator's word, as climb batch 13b; its gate is explorations/compile-ladder/climb-batch-13b/gate/. Edits the original tree: TraitTable.scala, TypeAnalyzer.scala.

